-- title:
--   Lemma 6.1, p. 23 (uniform form) — cost-to-go inequality with one constant c_6 for all stationary points
-- statement:
--   This is the cost-to-go inequality of Lemma 6.1 in the form its proof actually delivers: one constant serves **every** stationary point at once.
--
--   Work in the standing setting of Theorem 4.1 of the paper: problem (P) satisfies Assumptions 1 and 2, the step bound $\delta_k$ is set by rule (8), and $w^k=(u^k,v^k,p^k)$ is generated by NAPP-AL. Let $\mathcal L_\gamma$ be the augmented Lagrangian and call $\bar w$ a stationary point when $0\in\partial\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)$. Then there is a constant $c_6>0$ such that for every stationary point $\bar w$ and every $k\ge 0$,
--
--   $$
--   \mathcal L_\gamma(w^{k+1})-\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)\;\le\;c_6\big(\|\bar w-w^{k+1}\|^2+\|w^k-w^{k+1}\|^2\big).
--   $$
--
--   The paper states Lemma 6.1 for a fixed stationary point, but its proof assembles $c_6$ from the bounds (39)–(43), which involve only $L_G$, $L_H$, $L^0_\Theta$, $L_\Omega$, $L_K$, $\gamma$, $\|B\|$, a bound on $\|q^k\|$ (from the boundedness of $\{w^k\}$, Theorem 4.1(ii)) and a lower bound $\epsilon>0$ on the steps $\epsilon^k$; none of these depends on $\bar w$. The uniform form is what the proof of Proposition 6.2 needs, since there Lemma 6.1 is applied with $\bar w$ replaced by a point $w^{k+1}_p$ of the stationary set that changes with $k$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The order of quantifiers is $\exists c_6\,\forall \bar w\,\forall k$, which is stronger than the milestone statement `NAPPAL.Subreg.lemma_6_1` ($\forall\bar w\,\exists c_6\,\forall k$) and implies it. Norms on $(u,v,p)$ are the Euclidean norm of the stacked vector.
-- source:
--   Zhu, Zhao, Zhang, A First-Order Primal-Dual Method for Nonconvex Constrained Optimization Based on the Augmented Lagrangian, arXiv:2007.12219v1, pp. 23-26, Lemma 6.1, eq. (37) and its proof (38)-(43); used with a varying stationary point in the proof of Proposition 6.2, eq. (44), p. 26

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_Subreg_Setting

namespace NAPPAL.Subreg

open NAPPAL.Rate (qseq)
open NAPPAL.KL (wseq)

theorem lemma_6_1_uniform {n d m : ℕ} (P : NAPPAL.KL.Problem n d m) (LG LH L0 : ℝ) (LOmj : Fin m → ℝ)
    (LK : ℝ) (K : NAPPAL.KL.E n → ℝ) (β γ σ : ℝ) (δ ε : ℕ → ℝ)
    (u : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E n) (v : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E d) (p : ℕ → NAPPAL.KL.E m)
    (hrun : RunHyp P LG LH L0 LOmj LK K β γ σ δ ε u v p) :
    ∃ c6 : ℝ, 0 < c6 ∧ ∀ wbar : NAPPAL.KL.W n d m, NAPPAL.KL.IsStationary P γ wbar → ∀ k : ℕ,
      NAPPAL.KL.augLag P γ (wseq u v p (k+1)) - NAPPAL.KL.augLag P γ wbar ≤
        c6 * (NAPPAL.KL.wdist wbar (wseq u v p (k+1)) ^ 2 +
          NAPPAL.KL.wdist (wseq u v p k) (wseq u v p (k+1)) ^ 2) := by sorry

end NAPPAL.Subreg
